    "target_environment_scope": "target-owned /absolute/target/bin/kimi with isolated HOME, TMPDIR, and KIMI_CODE_HOME; credentials, sessions, logs, skills, agents, plugins, MCP, updates, and runtime data stay under the explicit target",
    "pre_login_supported": true,
    "lifecycle_lock_scope": "Target-bound mutation and launch acquire the persistent external product anchor first before target filesystem observation, canonicalization runs under that product handoff, the canonical target anchor is opened or published under exclusive product coordination, product coordination is released after target-anchor handoff, target-local internal lock is acquired second for mutations and launch, and locks are held from launch preflight through child process completion and cleanup; internal is released first and external target locks last. Read-only commands create no product or target anchor; cold no-anchor reads use the contract's double-check path, and seeded reads open existing anchors without creation.",
    "mutable_runtime_paths": "The managed target root, runtime HOME, runtime TMPDIR, KIMI_CODE_HOME, config, session, plugin, MCP, and log locations remain writable by the launched CLI",
